---
// Claims-boundary caveats for the TiC pricing-slice lab. Rendered beside every
// visual; wording is governed by docs/analysis/007-tic-anatomy-lab-claims-brief.md.
import { loadRelease } from "@lib/tic-pricing-slice";

const release = loadRelease();
const meta = release.source_metadata;
---

<aside class="caveats" aria-label="What this data cannot tell you">
  <p class="caveats-title">Before you read any number here as a price</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>These are July 2026 file contents, not current prices.</strong>
      Every fact is what specific {meta.payer} Colorado machine-readable files
      published for reporting month {meta.reporting_month}. Files carry no
      currentness claim.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>This is a bounded retained sample.</strong>
      {release.totals.row_count.toLocaleString("en-US")} retained facts across
      fifteen CPT codes — not a market, not all of the payer's rates, and not a
      completeness claim.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>USD is an assumption, not a source field.</strong> The source
      schema does not state a currency; the contract records the USD assumption
      explicitly.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Context is missing from this bounded slice.</strong> The CMS file
      format can carry billing-code modifiers, setting, and plan context, and
      the underlying files publish some of it — but this slice omits modifiers
      and setting, and plan attribution was not observed in it. Matching CPT
      codes alone do not establish comparable services.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>One dot or row is one retained published fact — never one
      provider.</strong> Provider group ids are release-scoped opaque source
      contexts, not identities.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Not advice.</strong> Nothing on this page is consumer medical or
      purchasing advice.
    </li>
  </ul>
</aside>

<style>
  .caveats {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--amber);
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .caveats-title {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .caveats ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }

  .caveats li {
    margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .caveats li:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .caveats strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 680;
  }
</style>
